// Title:       CrashStealer macOS -- network egress to delivery and C2 infrastructure
// Id:          fa2c1e90-crashstealer-c2 (parallel to Suricata rules)
// MITRE:       T1041, T1071.001, T1102.001
// Reference:   https://securityaffairs.com/195278/malware/crashstealer-new-macos-infostealer-uses-signed-apps-to-evade-gatekeeper.html
//              https://www.jamf.com/blog/crashstealer-macos-infostealer-analysis/
// Author:      Jarmi
// Date:        2026-07-25
// Tested on:   Microsoft Defender XDR advanced hunting (DeviceNetworkEvents, macOS onboarded devices)
// FP notes:    werkbit.io and endpoint-api-v1.com are not known-good domains
//              in any legitimate baseline; a hit against these or the
//              hardcoded C2 IP is treated as high-confidence. If the C2 IP
//              is later reused by a different, unrelated service, re-verify
//              via passive DNS before alerting purely on IP recurrence.
DeviceNetworkEvents
| where Timestamp > ago(14d)
| where RemoteUrl has_any ("werkbit.io", "endpoint-api-v1.com", "cohezo.io", "cohezo.com", "cordinex.io")
    or RemoteIP == "179.43.166.242"
| project Timestamp, DeviceName, InitiatingProcessFileName, RemoteUrl, RemoteIP, RemotePort,
          InitiatingProcessCommandLine
| order by Timestamp desc
